WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.740
CI/CD pipelines help organizations deliver software quickly and consistently.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:13.320
However, speed alone is not enough when teams must demonstrate that delivery activities were controlled, reviewed, tested, and documented.

3
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:26.640
Audit readiness means the pipeline can produce credible evidence about who made a change, when it happened, what was tested, what approvals were required, and whether required security controls were followed.

4
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.640
A well-designed pipeline does not treat governance as paperwork added after deployment.

5
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:37.260
It builds accountability, traceability, and control evidence into normal engineering workflows.

6
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.620
This approach helps development speed and governance coexist.

7
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:50.040
Automation captures routine evidence, reduces manual scrambling during audits, and gives teams a clearer view of operational and compliance risk.
